.TH SAMOYED\-KISSDUMP 1

.SH NAME
samoyed\-kissdump \- Decode a captured KISS byte stream.


.SH SYNOPSIS
.B samoyed\-kissdump
[ \fIoptions\fR ] < \fIcapture\fR


.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsamoyed\-kissdump\fR reads a capture of the bytes exchanged with a KISS TNC
from standard input and describes what it contains.

For each frame it undoes the KISS framing, shows the command byte and port
number, decodes the AX.25 header (addresses, digipeater path with the H bits,
control and PID), and hands the information field to the APRS decoder where the
frame is APRS.

Malformed input is reported rather than skipped, since that is usually what is
being chased: an unterminated frame, a bad escape sequence, a frame too short
to hold an AX.25 header, and bytes that are not part of any frame are all
described.  The exit status is non-zero if anything was wrong.


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--hex"
Input is hexadecimal digits rather than raw bytes, such as
.B c0 00 82
or
.BR c00082 .
Whitespace is ignored, so it does not matter how the digits are laid out across
lines, but anything else is an error: the offsets and ASCII column of a hex dump
have to be cut away first, or they would be read as data.
.TP
.BI "--help"
Display help text.


.SH EXAMPLES
.P
.B samoyed\-kissdump < capture.bin
.P
.B samoyed\-kissdump --hex < capture.txt


.SH SEE ALSO
.BR samoyed-kissutil (1),
.BR samoyed-decode_aprs (1)
